fun use(g, f:(() { |%::Lin}-@ ()), h) {xlin; g(); f(); h()} use
stdout : fun : (() { |a::Lin}-> (), () { |a::Lin}-@ (), () { |a::Lin}-> b::Any) { |a::Lin}-> b::Any

Linear function annotation with CFL enabled
sig h : ((a::Any) -e-@ a::Any, a::Any) { |e::Lin}-> a::Any fun h(f, x) {xlin; f(x)}
stdout : () : ()
exit : 0

Non-linear use of linear function with CFL enabled
sig h : ((a::Any) -e-@ a::Any, a::Any) { |e::Lin}-> a::Any fun h(f, x) {xlin; f(f(x))}
stderr : @..*
exit : 1

Linear identity with CFL enabled
fun (x) {xlin; x}
stdout : fun : (a::Any) { |_::Lin}-> a::Any
exit : 0

Non-linear dup with CFL enabled
fun (x) {(x, x)}
stdout : fun : (a) -> (a, a)
exit : 0

Non-linear generalisation (1) with CFL enabled
{var x = A; ()}
stdout : () : ()
exit : 0

Non-linear generalisation (2) with CFL enabled
fun (r) {var (x=42|q) = r; ()}
stdout : @fun..*
exit : 0
